 "verdict": "The CometEls census dipole (n=270, d_par=+0.101) survives the discovery-footprint null -- preserving each aphelion's ecliptic latitude while isotropizing ecliptic longitude (p=0.00215) as it did the galactic-tide null (p=0.00295).  Under magnitude terciles, era terciles, and perihelion-distance terciles the lean stays positive in 9/9 bins, and a single common amplitude is consistent with every variable's partition (H p=0.878, era p=0.900, q p=0.466) -- the dipole is a population property, not a brightness, epoch, or perihelion-selection artefact."
